Eshu is both an MCP server and a CLI toolkit for code analysis.

For MCP Server Mode (AI assistants):
  Use 'eshu mcp setup' to configure your IDE
  (server launch stays in the core binary)

For CLI Toolkit Mode (direct usage):
  eshu index .     -- Index your current directory
  eshu list        -- List indexed repositories

Run 'eshu help' to see all available commands.

Usage:
  eshu [command]

Available Commands:
  add-package              Removed: package indexing is owned by the Go bootstrap runtime
  admin                    STUB: core-only repair stays in core
  analyze                  Graph relationships and code quality analysis
  answer-quality-scorecard Score captured answer evidence across API, MCP, CLI, and hosted surfaces
  assistant                STUB: project guidance stays in core
  change                   Inspect pre-change impact over Eshu evidence
  clean                    Removed: use admin cleanup flows instead
  competitive-parity       STUB: shipped-surface validator stays in core
  completion               Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  component                Manage optional Eshu components
  config                   Manage configuration settings
  delete                   Removed: use admin deletion flows instead
  demo                     STUB: demo lifecycle stays in core
  demo-benchmark           STUB: demo scorer stays in core
  docs                     STUB: docs verification stays in core
  doctor                   Run diagnostics to check system health and configuration
  ecosystem                Ecosystem-wide analysis (migrated to Go)
  evidence                 STUB: portable bundle client stays in core
  evidence-packet-dogfood  STUB: packet benchmark stays in core
  find                     Search and discover entities in the code graph
  first-run                STUB: guided onboarding stays in core
  first-run-benchmark      STUB: first-run scorer stays in core
  freshness                Inspect ingestion freshness and generation lifecycle
  graph                    STUB: sidecar lifecycle stays in core
  help                     Help about any command
  help                     Show the main help message
  hosted-onboard           STUB: team onboarding stays in core
  hosted-setup             STUB: first-connection flow stays in core
  i                        Shortcut for 'eshu index'
  index                    Index a local path into the code graph
  index-status             Show the latest checkpointed indexing status
  install                  STUB: backend tooling install stays in core
  investigation            STUB: evidence-packet export stays in core
  list                     List all indexed repositories
  ls                       Shortcut for 'eshu list'
  m                        Shortcut for 'eshu mcp setup'
  map                      Map a bounded code-to-cloud entity neighborhood
  mcp                      MCP server commands
  n                        Shortcut for 'eshu neo4j setup'
  neo4j                    Neo4j database configuration
  playbooks                List and resolve deterministic query playbooks
  query                    Execute a language query against indexed code
  report                   Render a deterministic operator digest for an explicit scope
  rm                       Shortcut for 'eshu delete'
  scan                     STUB: local-owner scan stays in core
  service-report           Compose a service intelligence report from a captured service-story response
  stats                    Show indexing statistics
  trace                    Trace code-to-runtime evidence
  unwatch                  Removed: watcher lifecycle is owned by the Go ingester runtime
  version                  Show the installed application version
  vuln-scan                STUB: vulnerability evidence client stays in core
  w                        STUB: shortcut for watcher lifecycle stays in core
  watch                    STUB: watcher lifecycle stays in core
  watching                 Removed: watcher lifecycle is owned by the Go ingester runtime
  workspace                Multi-repository workspace operations

Flags:
      --database string   Temporarily override database backend
  -h, --help              help for eshu
  -v, --version           Show the installed application version
  -V, --visual            Show results as interactive graph visualization

Use "eshu [command] --help" for more information about a command.
